    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\">I understand... There were <u>two</u> mistakes:<div><br></div><div>- <b>knit_expand</b> does not &quot;knit&quot;: it only replaces the delimited variables; thus the output of <b>knit_expand</b> is a Rnw file, not a tex file; and when <span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">\\</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,0,102);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">Sexpr</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">{</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">paste</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">knit</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">text </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,136);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">out</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">),</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"> collapse </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,136,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">&#39;\\n&#39;</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">)}</span> is executed in the first section, <i>value</i> is 2 (the last value of the loop) !  </div><div>- <b>knit_child</b> &quot;knits&quot;: it compiles the R code and then generates at tex file; therefore in my second section, <span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">\\</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,0,102);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">Sexpr</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">{</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">paste</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">knit</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">(</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">text </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,136);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">out</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">),</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"> collapse </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">=</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,0,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"> </span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(0,136,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">&#39;\\n&#39;</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;color:rgb(102,102,0);background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\">)} </span>is totally useless, because &quot;out&quot; is some pure LaTeX code, without R code, and there&#39;s nothing to &quot;knit&quot; ! </div><div><br></div><div>This is the correct way: </div><div><div><br></div><div style=\"border:1px solid rgb(187,187,187);word-wrap:break-word;background-color:rgb(250,250,250)\"><code><div></div></code></div></div></div>"
